<title>JAPAN: Japan buys 130,000 tonnes wheat, 20,000 barley.</title>
<headline>Japan buys 130,000 tonnes wheat, 20,000 barley.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Food Agency said on Thursday it bought 60,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, 50,000 of Canadian wheat and 20,000 of Australian wheat, and 20,000 tonnes of Australian barley at its weekly tender.</p>
<p>They are all for October shipment. The following is a breakdown (in tonnes):</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p> COUNTRY    QUANTITY</p>
<p> U.S.	 60,000    Hard Red Winter	  20,000</p>
<p>(Protein 13.5 pct)</p>
<p> Dark Northern Spring   40,000</p>
<p> Canada     50,000    1CW			  34,000</p>
<p> Durum			16,000</p>
<p> Australia  20,000    Standard White	   20,000</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p>Australia  20,000    Feed			 20,000</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
</text>
